 "title": "A $1 deal and a 5-cent Coke that lasted 70 years",
 "question": "5 cents for 70 years",
 "format": "tags",
 "description": "From 1886 to 1959, a Coke cost a nickel. In 1899 two lawyers got the bottling rights for $1 with syrup at a fixed price forever, Coke painted '5 cents' everywhere, and its vending machines took only a nickel. Coke's boss even asked President Eisenhower for a 7.5-cent coin.",
 "pillar": "money history",
 "hashtags": [
  "moneystory",
  "cocacola",
  "history"
 ],
 "comment": "Would you promise one price forever? 👇",
